From: James Calligeros <jcalligeros99@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: Adaptive Sync / ProMotion (VRR), behind appledrm.force_vrr

Backport of the seven commits at the top of chadmed/linux dcp/vrr
(AsahiLinux/linux pull request 477, not merged yet), squashed:

  23682c5d3cbd drm: apple: Do not set IOMFBParameter_adaptive_sync on poweron
  459e0490f7d5 drm: apple: Add preliminary VRR support
  11741c81a788 drm: apple: Force modeset when VRR is toggled
  67e5ae50952c drm: apple: Set swap timestamps to sane values for Adaptive Sync
  50830fcfe5aa drm: apple: Set min and max VRRs for MacBook Pros
  8836a0f2c7d9 drm: apple: Only use swap timestamps if VRR is actually active
  8a808006a701 NOUPSTREAM: drm: apple: Hide VRR behind a module parameter

DCP does VRR itself: it is switched on by setting the adaptive sync
parameter's minimum refresh rate and then setting the mode again, and
the refresh rate then follows the swap timestamps. With
appledrm.force_vrr=1, every mode set on a VRR-capable display (the
14/16-inch MacBook Pro panels at 120 Hz, 24 to 120 Hz; external
displays whose EDID gives a range) turns it on. KMS and the compositor
are not told (vrr_capable stays 0), because KMS forbids the mode set
DCP needs. Without the parameter the display runs as before.

Upstream marks this experimental: the pull request reports mpv's gpu
and gpu-next outputs halting the GPU in fullscreen on the internal
display.

Adjusted for asahi-7.2.14-1: the ns_to_mach() helper is added in front
of iomfb_flush(), whose signature here takes a drm_atomic_commit; the
rest applies with offsets. Builds without warnings against
7.2.14-p1-asahi-dist.

Signed-off-by: James Calligeros <jcalligeros99@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
